# getproperty-web — every environment variable this app reads (validated at boot by src/lib/env;
# an invalid value stops the server and lists every problem). Copy to .env.local for local work.
# Anything NEXT_PUBLIC_* is compiled into the browser bundle and is public by definition.
#
# Outside production the hosts and the API URL default to the values shown, so `pnpm dev` needs no
# .env at all. In production OWNER_HOST, STAFF_HOST, ADMIN_HOST and API_INTERNAL_URL are required.

# ── Zones (00-master-plan.md §2, ADR-0004) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Host header values (host[:port]), not URLs. The port is ignored when matching. Unknown hosts are 404.
OWNER_HOST=localhost:3002
STAFF_HOST=staff.localhost:3002
ADMIN_HOST=admin.localhost:3002

# Optional allow-list: which zones this deployment answers for (the others' hosts are 404).
# Unset means all three. There is no resident/LIFF zone here: that is getproperty-liff (D-154).
# ZONES=owner,staff

# Optional: the platform's public site (getproperty.app). It serves only the marketing pages
# (/, /pricing, /legal/*) and 308s every other path to OWNER_HOST; with it set, the owner host's
# copy of those pages is noindex and the canonical/sitemap URLs point here. Unset = as before.
# MARKETING_HOST=getproperty.localhost:3000

# ── Backend (getproperty-api) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-to-server only (Server Components, the zone BFFs, the proxy's token refresh). Browser code
# calls this app's own /bff/* instead. getproperty-api listens on :3000 by default — run it with
# PORT=4000 next to `pnpm dev`.
API_INTERNAL_URL=https://uat-api.getproperty.app
# Build-time only: where `pnpm gen:api --adopt` reads the contract from (contract.lock.json pins it).
API_CONTRACT_SOURCE=../getproperty-api/contract/openapi.json
# `pnpm dev:mock` starts the mock API (mocks/server.ts, port MOCK_API_PORT=4010) and points this at it.
# Proxies in front of this app that write X-Forwarded-For. On the Collective platform (D-230) that is Caddy alone = 1:
# it replaces the header of an internet client with the address it saw (and appends for a trusted one), so the
# right-most entry is the end user. The platform compose file (collective-infra platform/products/getproperty)
# sets TRUSTED_HOPS=1. The BFFs, Server Actions and Server Components send the API only the entry this many from
# the right, so the API's per-IP sign-in throttle, session rows, audit and D-021a acknowledgements record the user,
# not this container (review H1, api RUNBOOK §11, D-229). 0 = nothing is forwarded (local dev). Never more than
# the real number of hops: one too many lets a caller choose its address. A warning is logged at boot when it is
# 0 in production.
# TRUSTED_HOPS=1

# ── Public values ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Origin of signed object-storage / CDN URLs (meter photos, slips) — allowed by the CSP.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ASSET_BASE_URL=https://files.getproperty.co
# LINE Official Account id for the help link (a link only; no LINE SDK in this app).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LINE_OA_ID=@getproperty
# LIFF id of the resident / prospect LINE Mini App (getproperty-liff): a listing's contact button opens it at
# /rent/<slug> to ask the owner and book a viewing (D-252); unset = a chat with the LINE OA.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LIFF_ID=1657000000-AbCdEfGh
# VAPID application server key for web push; unset = read from GET /v1/auth/web-push/public-key.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# Environment badge in every shell (uat, staging…); unset or "production" shows none.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ENV_BADGE=uat

# ── Observability (F1 1.3) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SENTRY_DSN=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=uat
# SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=0
# OTLP/HTTP collector for server traces (fetch spans to getproperty-api carry `traceparent`).
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=getproperty-web
